# REVIEW.md — <Repo name>

How to review a change in this repo, for AI reviewers (`/arffornia:review`, the
`arffornia:reviewer` agent) and humans. Keep it short and specific to this repo.

## Output
- First line: `Findings: N (blocking b, major m, minor k) · risk: high|medium|low`.
- Every finding cites `path:line` and the evidence (quoted code, or a command and its output).
  No evidence: ask a question instead.
- At most 3 style remarks. Formatting belongs to `make fmt`, not to review.
- End with a verdict: approve, request changes, or comment. Say what you did not verify.

## Depth by risk
| Risk | Paths in this repo | Depth |
|---|---|---|
| High | <auth, secrets, network input, release workflows, ...> | Every line, trace callers, try to break it |
| Medium | <business logic, persistence, ...> | Every line, check tests cover it |
| Low | <docs, tests only, ...> | Skim |

## Always check
- The change matches its issue's acceptance criteria and does nothing else.
- `make check` output is in the PR; a test fails without the change.
- <Repo-specific invariants, e.g. "every HTTP call has a timeout".>

## Skip
- <Generated files, lockfiles, vendored code, ...>
